Z||000011||Standard||02-14-2000||01:18 AM||||Daved,<BR>If you had #921 bulbs in there, they were not stock!  921's can melt the socket!  they run on 12.8 volts and 1.4 amps, which is 70 watts total for the 4 of them!  <P>The standard bulb is a #194, which uses 14 volts at .27 amps.  The 906 is a <B>much</B> better choice, although they are darker than 921's, they won't melt the socket. <A HREF="http://members.xoom.com/fierov6/OSG/mod.PONTIAC-lights.html" TARGET=_blank>http://members.xoom.com/fierov6/OSG/mod.PONTIAC-lights.html</A> ||||reg||4
Z||000012||Eddie.H||02-14-2000||08:32 PM|||| Batboy In  NJ they would towe your car for that. its cool looking I wish I could do some thing like that. Eddie ||||reg||6
Z||000013||daved||02-14-2000||10:34 PM||||Standard, I stand...corrected. You lot sure are sharp! Misread the notes from Online Service.  Stock is as you say, #194.  But I did put in the #906, which is brighter and takes 0.69 Amps. Very pleased with the results, and no melting of sockets.  ||||reg||1
Z||000014||Standard||02-14-2000||11:40 PM||||No problem, man.  I want brighter lights too, but I replaced mine with the stock 194's because... uhhhh... actauly 'cause I was too lazy to look for any other bulbs.  oh well.. I have other things I need to spend money on for that car..  ||||reg||7
